 Initialise connected;who;i
⍝ Called once per browser connection, in a thread of its own
⍝ (Handler.aplf:46 — app._EWC.TID←(app⍎fn)&CONNECTED). Must be monadic;
⍝ Init.aplf:58 refuses to start Multi mode without it.
⍝
⍝ Every widget here exists to make a server-side fact assertable from
⍝ Playwright. The form renders each APL id as a DOM id, so a test locates
⍝ #F1\.WHOAMI and reads this clone's own name straight out of the page.
⍝
⍝ Errors in this function suspend the detached thread, which reads to a
⍝ test as a hang. So the Form and WHOAMI are created from statements that
⍝ cannot fail, and everything after is trapped: a failure then shows up as
⍝ an assertable caption instead of a timeout.
⍝
⍝ Note what this function deliberately does NOT do: the demos all open with
⍝ `EWC.CONNECTED←connected`, which writes a global on the single shared
⍝ #.EWC from every session. In a fixture whose entire purpose is proving
⍝ isolation, writing shared state on connect would be self-defeating —
⍝ and it is redundant, since Init.aplf:84 already sets CONNECTED←1.

 ⍝ Per-clone state. NOT localised, on purpose — these become variables of
 ⍝ #.mtest_N, and proving they are not shared is what isolation.spec.ts
 ⍝ exists to do.
 count←0
 private←'-'
 refreshes←0

 'F1'eWC'Form'('EWC Multi Test — ',⍕⎕THIS)(50 50)(400 520)('Coord' 'Pixel')
 'F1.WHOAMI'eWC'Label'(⍕⎕THIS)(10 10)(23 500)

 :Trap 0
     who←'-'
     :If 2=_EWC.⎕NC'QUERY'
     :AndIf (≢_EWC.QUERY)≥i←_EWC.QUERY[;1]⍳⊂'who'
         who←⊃_EWC.QUERY[i;2]
     :EndIf

     'F1.T1'eWC'Label' 'Session:'(45 10)(23 130)
     'F1.SESSIONID'eWC'Label'(⍕_EWC.ID)(45 150)(23 120)
     'F1.T2'eWC'Label' 'Thread:'(45 280)(23 90)
     'F1.TID'eWC'Label'(⍕⎕TID)(45 380)(23 120)

     'F1.T3'eWC'Label' 'Query who:'(75 10)(23 130)
     'F1.QUERY'eWC'Label'who(75 150)(23 350)

     'F1.T4'eWC'Label' 'Private:'(105 10)(23 130)
     'F1.PRIVATEIN'eWC'Edit' ''(105 150)(23 200)('Style' 'Single')
     'F1.SETPRIVATE'eWC'Button' 'Set'(105 360)(23 140)('Event' 'Select' 'CBSetPrivate')
     'F1.PRIVATE'eWC'Label'private(135 150)(23 350)

     'F1.T5'eWC'Label' 'Counter:'(170 10)(23 130)
     'F1.COUNTER'eWC'Label'(⍕count)(170 150)(23 120)
     'F1.INC'eWC'Button' 'Increment'(170 280)(23 140)('Event' 'Select' 'CBIncrement')

     'F1.T6'eWC'Label' 'Clones:'(210 10)(23 130)
     'F1.CLONES'eWC'Label'(cloneList ⍬)(210 150)(23 350)

     'F1.T7'eWC'Label' 'Closed:'(240 10)(23 130)
     'F1.CLOSELOG'eWC'Label'(closeList ⍬)(240 150)(23 350)

     'F1.REFRESH'eWC'Button' 'Refresh'(275 10)(23 140)('Event' 'Select' 'CBRefresh')
     'F1.RUNPROBE'eWC'Button' 'Run WG probe'(275 160)(23 160)('Event' 'Select' 'CBProbe')

     ⍝ Refresh sequence number, written LAST by CBRefresh. A test cannot tell
     ⍝ a stale CLONES value from a fresh one just by looking at it, so it
     ⍝ watches this instead: WebSocket frames are applied in order, so once
     ⍝ this changes the two captions above it are already up to date.
     'F1.REFRESHN'eWC'Label'(⍕refreshes)(275 340)(23 60)

     'F1.T8'eWC'Label' 'Probe:'(310 10)(23 130)
     'F1.PROBE'eWC'Label' '-'(310 150)(23 350)

     ⍝ The WG probe target. Caption on a Label is NOT dynamic
     ⍝ (classes/label/Dynamic.apla is empty), so dWG answers it from APL
     ⍝ state without ever asking the browser. Edit's Text IS dynamic, so
     ⍝ reading this forces a real client round-trip through the per-session
     ⍝ ⎕TGET/⎕TPUT rendezvous — which is the thing concurrency.spec.ts
     ⍝ exists to stress. Seeded with the clone name so a reply routed to
     ⍝ the wrong session is self-evident. Tests never type into it.
     'F1.T9'eWC'Label' 'Token:'(340 10)(23 130)
     'F1.TOKEN'eWC'Edit'(⍕⎕THIS)(340 150)(23 350)('Style' 'Single')
 :Else
     'F1.WHOAMI'eWS'Caption'('INIT ERROR: ',⊃⎕DMX.DM)
 :EndTrap

 ⍝ Multi mode requires the session thread to sit in ⎕DQ, exactly as
 ⍝ demo/Initialise.aplf:13-15 does. Without this the thread returns, the
 ⍝ session's event pump stops, and the page goes dead on first click.
 eDQ'F1'
